iginal not acquired in this batch.","transport_layer_context_m":[0,1000]},"adjacent_stream_span_is_north_pacific_width":false,"adjacent_stream_transport_layer_is_width_layer":false,"alternative_43N_split_is_velocity_boundary":false,"audit_file":"research/north-pacific-tomczak-2005-broad-band-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"09ec3af553122962de08298c120113149d1c822857cd80fb3381fcc15c9e235a","cross_current_width_inheritance_eligible":false,"description_kind":"broad-combined-eastward-flow-band","display_aria_label":"North Pacific Current: source reports a broad combined eastward flow band more than 2000 kilometres wide. Textbook synthesis using a broad combined definition; representative width, paired boundaries, layer, observation dates and numerical uncertainty unknown. No finite or seasonal width range.","display_caption":"More than 2000 km · broad combined eastward flow band in the textbook’s North Pacific definition. Representative width and numerical uncertainty unknown; no selected 2000 km point, finite interval or annual range.","display_constraint_label":"Broad eastward flow band","display_method_note":"Original PDF p135 inspected, chapter page version March 2005. The source combines Kuroshio/Oyashio continuations and discusses an alternative North Pacific/Subarctic split. Adjacent Alaskan Stream 150–200 km and upper-kilometer transport layer are separate; no width boundaries or seasonal calendar extracted.","display_title":"Reported broad flow band","front_latitudes_are_width_edges":false,"full_book_reviewed":false,"map_buffer_eligible":false,"more_than_scale_is_representative_width":false,"more_than_scale_is_rigorous_bound":false,"naming_context":{"alaskan_stream_is_aleutian_alias":false,"alternative_definition":"Some authors split North Pacific south of about 43°N and Pacific Subarctic Current north of it. Source questions persistence of this separation across basin.","canonical_names_changed":false,"canonical_subarctic_current_id":"aleutian","combined_brea